 \nThe landlord has **1 card left**, so saving our highest card (BlackJoker) to beat their last card when they are forced to lead is crucial.  \nIf we use BlackJoker now, we give landlord the chance to win after our play (we lead with a pair, landlord could pass, teammate might not be able to take over).  \nIf we pass and teammate beats ♥9, we keep our rocket piece for a guaranteed stop later.  \nOnly risk: if teammate cannot beat ♥9, landlord wins immediately next turn.  \nBut with 8 cards, it’s very likely teammate has something higher than 9.  \n\nThus passing here maximizes team’s control — we trust teammate to beat a small single ♥9, then we can save BlackJoker for landlord’s final move.\n\n**Answer:**  \n{"cards": []}'}
